## S1. G on negative integers coprime to 3: cycles and basins
S1.1 G(-p) = -G_-(p) with the same k for all p <= 20000, 3 !| p; k-tables k_+(r)={1: 2, 2: 1, 4: 0, 5: 3, 7: 0, 8: 1}, k_-(r)={1: 1, 2: 0, 4: 3, 5: 0, 7: 1, 8: 2}, k_-(r) = k_+(-r mod 9).
S1.2 G(-1) = -1 (k=1); G(-4) = -11 (k=3); G(-11) = -4 (k=0).
S1.2 gate: m0=-1 word=(1,) (J,L)=(1,1) 2^J-3^L=-1 B'=1
S1.2 gate: m0=-4 word=(3, 0) (J,L)=(3,2) 2^J-3^L=-1 B'=4
