## S3. G-analogue of the bounded-strip theorem: numerical anchors
S3.1 sum_{s=1}^{300} 3^s/2^{K_s} < 3 m_0 verified for every positive m_0 <= 5000; largest ratio (sum)/m_0 = 3.000000 at m_0 = 1 (bound 3).
S3.2a G_- words of length J are functions of m mod 3^(J+1) for J <= 6 (all unit classes, lifts t=1,2,5).
S3.2b G_-: E_Haar[2^{K_J}] = 3(7/3)^(J-1) exactly, B_J <= 2^{K_J}(3^J-1)/2 on every class, and Haar{2^{K_J} >= 3^J/2} <= 2(7/9)^(J-1), J <= 8:
